  "body": "Found during the review of PR #839 (#689).\n\n**What:** the programs behind `contour_disc_hole` and `contour_tangential_lead` are refused by the program gate for crossing lead-in/lead-out moves (true on main before #839 as well - `solid_law_goldens` pins the refusal). Yet posted NC goldens for them are kept under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/<dialect>/` in every dialect and are compared by `conformance`.\n\n**Why it matters:** a golden of posted G-code for a program the gate would never let a user post reads as \"this output is right\". It also makes every arc-fit or lead change regenerate goldens that describe output no user can get.\n\n**Options:** (a) fix the two fixtures so their programs pass the gate (move the lead so it no longer crosses) and keep the goldens; (b) keep the fixtures as refusal pins only and drop their posted goldens from the dialect sets; (c) post them only through a test-only path that says \"refused program, posted for syntax conformance\" in the golden's header.\n\nDone means: no posted golden exists for a program the gate refuses, or each such golden says so in its first line and a test pins that the gate still refuses it.\n\nEffort is `high` under the safety floor (posted G-code goldens and the post gate).\n",
